Document the usage and caveats of setting the imageRegistry config as well as image / imageContext and imageTag options for custom name / context and tag.

Caveats to note:

If will not create a new IS if;
a) you already have an imagestream in the namespace or;
b) the samples operator created the imagestreams in the openshift namespace

Its noted in the CRD and the console:
https://github.com/kiegroup/kie-cloud-operator/blob/main/deploy/crds/kieapp.crd.yaml#L340
And
https://github.com/kiegroup/kie-cloud-operator/blob/main/deploy/crds/kieapp.crd.yaml#L589-L597

But imageRegistry is not in the actual documentation.

When successful, you will see the operator create the desired imagstream using your custom registry:

{code}
{"level":"warn","ts":"2021-10-20T13:43:38.730449242Z","logger":"kieapp.controller","msg":"ImageStreamTag openshift/rhdm-kieserver-rhel8:7.11.1 doesn't exist."}
{"level":"info","ts":"2021-10-20T13:43:38.730548169Z","logger":"kieapp.controller","msg":"Creating","kind":"ImageStreamTag","name":"rhdm-kieserver-rhel8:7.11.1","from":"matt.registry.io/rhdm-7/rhdm-kieserver-rhel8:7.11.1","namespace":"cigna-dm"}
{code}

